{"title":"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems\">2006 AMC 12A #12</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">2006 AMC 10A #14</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Brute_force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Brute force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A number of linked rings, each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm thick, are hanging on a peg. The top ring has an outside diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm. The outside diameter of each of the outer rings is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm less than that of the ring above it. The bottom ring has an outside diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm. What is the distance, in cm, from the top of the top ring to the bottom of the bottom ring?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75b3e762b96f49323740d90a83fdb1339789180e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm); pathpen = linewidth(0.7); D(CR((0,0),10)); D(CR((0,0),9.5)); D(CR((0,-18.5),9.5)); D(CR((0,-18.5),9)); MP(&quot;$\\vdots$&quot;,(0,-31),(0,0)); D(CR((0,-39),3)); D(CR((0,-39),2.5)); D(CR((0,-43.5),2.5)); D(CR((0,-43.5),2)); D(CR((0,-47),2)); D(CR((0,-47),1.5)); D(CR((0,-49.5),1.5)); D(CR((0,-49.5),1.0));  D((12,-10)--(12,10)); MP(&#39;20&#39;,(12,0),E); D((12,-51)--(12,-48)); MP(&#39;3&#39;,(12,-49.5),E);[/asy]\" width=\"148\" height=\"332\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa6459ccc9fd6e39b0316f7caf4db43a04046004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 171\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 173\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 182\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 188\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 210\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"479\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The inside diameters of the rings are the positive integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  The total distance needed is the sum of these values plus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for the top of the first ring and the bottom of the last ring. Using the formula for the sum of an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_series\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Arithmetic series\">arithmetic series</a>, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a14d734ec4163ca7028761cc482f869f37298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{18 \\cdot 19}{2} + 2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }173}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"184\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alternatively, the sum of the consecutive integers from 3 to 20 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9c64de6e13f7680458b39641f7be0cf2005045d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(18)(3+20) = 207$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"160\" height=\"37\" />.  However, the 17 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Intersection\" title=\"Intersection\">intersections</a> between the rings must be subtracted, and we also get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c8a2d702906f58de5f50f564c3d83691d67743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$207 - 2(17) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }173}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"190\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Brute_force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Brute_force)\">Solution 3 (Brute force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Brute force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can just add all the numbers up. But, we have to account for the intersections, so the final expression is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a515f2e1b17253fba1d96677bbd80bca363e284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+\\sum_{k=2}^{18} k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"56\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/656f75b4e36a24b4de9227b0ac34120c017d6199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }173}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />. ~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shunyipanda&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Shunyipanda (page does not exist)\">shunyipanda</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A\">2006 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Probl